# The live stage of the guide to writing a package: the same code as the
# package, as a config file (`config/Config/WordCount.lean`) that
# `config/init.lean` imports. The reload's count, 2 files and 1 command,
# says config's module was elaborated and its `setup` registered
# `word-count`, and the command runs. The fixture set's editor also links
# the package, whose command prints the same, so this does not show which
# ran; that config's command of a name runs in place of a package's is
# pinned by `ModelTest.packageChecks` ("config's command of a package's
# command's name runs in its place ..."). It touches no file.

reload
settle

key i KeyI -
commit one two  three
key <Escape> Escape -
run word-count
scene
